<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 18th century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 1700s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/18th-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 1750 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 9988 5257" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 1750 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="4997" cy="651" r="170"/><text x="4997" y="722" font-size="204">1</text></g><g><circle cx="7567" cy="1068" r="170"/><text x="7567" y="1139" font-size="204">2</text></g><g><circle cx="5709" cy="970" r="170"/><text x="5709" y="1042" font-size="204">3</text></g><g><circle cx="2321" cy="1717" r="170"/><text x="2321" y="1788" font-size="204">4</text></g><g><circle cx="6487" cy="457" r="170"/><text x="6487" y="528" font-size="204">5</text></g><g><circle cx="7018" cy="1385" r="170"/><text x="7018" y="1456" font-size="204">6</text></g><g><circle cx="4773" cy="1044" r="170"/><text x="4773" y="1116" font-size="204">7</text></g><g><circle cx="8530" cy="1145" r="170"/><text x="8530" y="1216" font-size="204">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 1750 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Qing Empire &middot; Russian Empire &middot; British Empire &middot; Ottoman Empire &middot; Tokugawa Shogunate &middot; Mughal Empire &middot; Portuguese Empire &middot; New Spain</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Treaty of Campo Formio</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Acts of Union 1707</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>War of the Spanish Succession</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Treaty of Utrecht</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Treaty of Paris (1763)</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>French Revolution</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Peter the Great</li><li>Maria Theresa</li><li>Usman dan Fodio</li><li>Catherine the Great</li><li>Frederick the Great</li><li>Voltaire</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1717–1780</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1712–1786</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1672–1725</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1754–1817</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1729–1796</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1694–1778</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 1700s, 407 recorded states were founded and 339 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the British Empire, the Qing Empire and the Ottoman Empire. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 18th century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/18th-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 18th century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>British Empire <span>1583 CE – 1997 CE</span></li><li>Qing Empire <span>1644 CE – 1912 CE</span></li><li>Ottoman Empire <span>1299 CE – 1922 CE</span></li><li>New Spain <span>1521 CE – 1821 CE</span></li><li>Russian Empire <span>1721 CE – 1917 CE</span></li><li>Mughal Empire <span>1526 CE – 1857 CE</span></li><li>Portuguese Empire <span>1415 CE – 1975 CE</span></li><li>Tokugawa Shogunate <span>1603 CE – 1868 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>War of the Spanish Succession <span>1701–1714</span></li><li>Acts of Union 1707 <span>1707</span></li><li>Treaty of Utrecht <span>1713</span></li><li>Treaty of Paris (1763) <span>1763</span></li><li>French Revolution <span>1789–1799</span></li><li>Treaty of Campo Formio <span>1797</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Peter the Great <span>3: 1672–1725</span></li><li>Maria Theresa <span>1: 1717–1780</span></li><li>Usman dan Fodio <span>4: 1754–1817</span></li><li>Catherine the Great <span>5: 1729–1796</span></li><li>Frederick the Great <span>2: 1712–1786</span></li><li>Voltaire <span>6: 1694–1778</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
